+# Discount codes
+
+## Request
+
+> Marketing want to run promotions with discount codes.
+> Start with percentage-off codes: staff create them, with an optional expiry date, and customers can enter one at checkout.
+> We'll probably want other kinds of promotion later (a fixed amount off, free shipping, buy one get one free), so bear that in mind.
+
+## Commits
+
+1. `feat`: staff can create percentage-off discount codes (service, with an audit entry).
+   - New migration `008_discount_codes.sql`: a `discount_codes` table keyed by `code`, with a `kind` column (`percent` for now) and a nullable `percent`, so other kinds can add their own columns in later migrations without reshaping this one.
+   - `DiscountCode` in `shop/domain/models.py` has a `kind` too. I'm not building a class hierarchy or registry for kinds we don't have yet.
+   - Codes are case-insensitive: stored and looked up upper-case, 3 to 20 of `A-Z`, `0-9` and `-`. A duplicate is a `Conflict`.
+   - The percentage must be 1 to 100.
+   - Expiry is a date (`expires_on`), not a time: the code works up to the end of that day in UK time (`clock.SHOP_TIMEZONE`). An expiry date already in the past is rejected.
+   - Audited as `discount_code.created`, subject `discount_code:<CODE>`.
+2. `feat`: `POST /admin/discount-codes` lets staff create a code over the API.
+   - Body `{"code", "percent", "expires_on"}` (`expires_on` optional, `YYYY-MM-DD`). Returns 201 with the code.
+   - Only create, no list/update/delete: not asked for yet.
+3. `feat`: a discount code becomes an `Adjustment` of kind `discount_code`, and expired codes are rejected (domain only).
+   - The percentage is of the merchandise before other adjustments, like the employee discount, so the order they're applied in doesn't matter.
+   - Description like `"SUMMER20: 20% off"`, so the order records which code was used without adding a field to orders.
+4. `feat`: customers can enter a discount code when placing an order (service).
+   - One code per order.
+   - Codes stack with the employee discount and loyalty points. If together they come to more than the merchandise, `price` already rejects the order.
+   - An unknown or expired code is a `ValidationFailed` (422), not a 404: it's a bad value in the request, not a missing resource.
+   - No usage limits (per customer or overall): not asked for.
+5. `feat`: `POST /checkout` accepts an optional `discount_code`.
+   - The cart preview doesn't take a code yet.
+
+Later promotions, for reference (not built): a fixed amount off fits as another `kind` that makes an `Adjustment`. Free shipping doesn't fit `Adjustment` (which comes off merchandise, before tax), so it will need a change to `pricing.price`. Buy one get one free needs the order lines, so the code-to-adjustment function will take the lines rather than just the merchandise total when that comes.
